.\" Written by go test ./test -update, from rayo help all
.TH RAYO 1 "" rayo "rayo help all"
.SH START HERE: THE FAST, CHEAP WAY TO USE RAYO
.nf
For anyone driving rayo, a person or a program. The cheapest step that answers the question first.

Know before you run
  rayo check <flows>, no device and instant: the plan, and every mistake. Fix all it says, then run.

Run the smallest unit
  One flow, not the suite: rayo test --only <name> --retries 0 --fail-fast <suite>.

Read the cause, not the logs
  A failure leads with its verdict, <flow> failed at <step>: <cause>, and a blame of test, app or
  device. --detail brief is that alone; rayo explain says it again for the last run, without one.
  Open the recordings, logcat or calls in --output only if the verdict isn't enough.

A failure is information, not a reason to rerun (by its blame)
  device: fix the environment; the same flow on a broken device only costs time.
  app: a crash or a hang of the app, a finding to report.
  test: the flow or the mocks are wrong; fix them. Retry only what a retry can change.

Batch edits, then verify once
  Make all the changes, rayo check --changed-only, run the narrowest unit, then
  rayo test --rerun-failed.
  Don't rerun flows that passed to be sure.

Author forward
  rayo live <flow>, then rayo do --screen --find <text> <command>: one command, see only the
  elements that matter, go on from it. rayo do --screen=changes gives only the lines that
  appeared (+) or went (-) since the last screen: after - waitForAnimationToEnd, as --screen
  doesn't wait for a screen still moving; --ignore-screen <regex> leaves out a clock.
  rayo do --timeout 2m never waits for ever. rayo do .save says the lines it wrote and checks them.
  rayo do .quit ends the session and frees the device; with steps not saved, only with --discard.

Stop after a pass

Prefer structured output
  When a program reads: --format json or ndjson, --detail brief, --show failed, --keep failed.

What it costs, roughly
  rayo check        instant, no device
  one flow          seconds to minutes
  a whole suite     many minutes
  a capture         slow; it makes new ids, so diffs are noisy
  rayo live         holds the device until it ends

I want to...
  write a flow                         rayo help write-a-flow
  find why a flow failed               rayo explain, then rayo help debug-a-flow
  go on from a failure, after a fix    rayo test --resume <suite>; rayo help resume
  record a video                       record: true in the header; rayo help recipes
  check the device log, reset the app  rayo help recipes
  mock the backend                     rayo help record-mocks, rayo help connect-mocks
  run in a CI                          rayo help run-in-ci
  find any word in the help            rayo help search <word>
.fi
.SH COMMANDS AND OPTIONS
.nf
rayo - runs flows on Android, fast

New here, or driving rayo from a program? Start with: rayo help agents

  rayo test [options] <flow, folder or suite>...   run flows; a suite is a *.suite.yaml
  rayo check <flow, folder or suite>...            check flows without a device, and say which would run
  rayo explain [<run folder or flow>]              why the flows of the last run failed, in a few lines
  rayo live [options] <flow>                       write a flow as it runs, command by command
  rayo do [options] <commands>                     send commands to the live session; rayo do .help
  rayo hierarchy [options]                         what is on screen, and how to refer to it
  rayo devices                                     connected devices
  rayo mocks apply [options] <folder>              take the changes of rayo test --capture-update into the mocks
  rayo mocks import [options] <file.har> <folder>  write the calls of a HAR file, such as mitmproxy's, as mocks
  rayo mocks check <folder>                        mappings that never answer, and bodies no mapping uses
  rayo ca new [<folder>]                           a CA for the project, in .rayo/ca, to commit with the flows
  rayo ca export <file>                            the certificate the proxy signs with, for the app's debug build
  rayo help <command>                              what a command takes, of a flow or of rayo; or <command> --help
  rayo help <topic>                                flow, suite, json, all (everything on one page), or a topic below
  rayo help search <word>...                       the lines of all the help that have the words
  rayo schema <name>                               a JSON Schema: flow, suite, results, or of --format json
  rayo version

Topics, rayo help <topic>
  agents                     start here: the fast, cheap way to use rayo
  write-a-flow               write a flow
  debug-a-flow               debug a failing flow
  resume                     go on from where a flow failed, after a fix, without running it all again
  record-mocks               record mocks from the real backend
  connect-mocks              connect the app to the mocks: interceptor or proxy
  run-in-ci                  run in a CI
  recipes                    short answers: video, logcat, reset, log in, deeplink, what a run leaves
  limits                     limitations and gotchas
  exit-codes                 exit codes

Options of test, live and hierarchy
  --device <serial>          when several are connected
  --emulator                 never a real device, even if it is the only one

Options of test and check: which flows
  --changed-only             only the flows of which a file changed: their own, one they run, or a mock; as --since HEAD
  --since <git ref>          only the flows of which a file changed since then, also not committed

Options of hierarchy and do
  --find <text>              of the screen, only the elements most like it, instead of all

Options of test, live, do and explain
  --output <folder>          where failures and screenshots go (default .rayo)

Options of test and live
  --timeout-scale <factor>   multiply the default waits, not a step's own timeout (default 1)
  --mock-port <port>         where the app finds the mock on the device (default 8080)
  --animations               leave the device's animations on
  --profile                  where the time of each step went

Options of test and check: which flows of them
  --only <a,b>               only the flows with these names
  --include-tags <a,b>       only flows with one of these tags
  --exclude-tags <a,b>       not flows with one of these tags
  --rerun-failed             only those that haven't passed since they last failed
  --shard <i/n>              only part i of n, for n machines that run the same flows: each flow is in one part, by its path, whatever the order

Options of test and check: as the suite says, for one run
  -e, --env <KEY=VALUE>      a variable for the flows; over the suite's env, which is over a flow's own
  --retries <n>              try again what fails, every flow, also one the suite gives its own retries (default 1, or the suite's)

Options of test: how they run
  --fail-fast                stop at the first failure
  --flaky-fails-build        exit 4 if every flow passed but some only on a retry (default: exit 0)
  --keep-going               don't stop when the device or the app fails over and over
  --shuffle[=seed]           in a random order, or in that of an earlier run
  -c, --continuous           run again whenever a file changes

Options of test: from where, after a fix; see rayo help resume
  --resume                   each flow that failed last time, from the step that failed, with the app as it is and the mocks' scenarios as they were then
  --from <step>              begin one flow at a step: file:line as rayo explain's at: says, a line of its own file, or a text of one step such as pickDate; the app is as it is, onFlowStart doesn't run
  --until <step>             stop one flow after a step, given as --from takes it, leaving the app there; onFlowComplete doesn't run
  --mock-state <a=s,b=t>     with --resume or --from, the scenarios' states to begin with, over those of the last run

Options of test and check: what is written, as the suite's output
  --video                    a video of each flow whose header doesn't say record, as output: { video: true }
  --keep <when>              the files of every try (all, default), only of the tries that failed, or none
  --artifacts <a,b>          the kinds of file written: video, screenshot, logcat, screen, requests (default all)
  --name-template <template> how the files are named in the output folder (default {flow}_{attempt}_{kind}.{ext})

Options of test: what comes out
  --detail <how much>        printed: brief, the verdict of a failure; normal (default), also why, where, the nearest elements and the calls, and every step of a single flow; full, also the screen, every step, and whole files
  --failure-window <seconds> a failure's log and calls begin this long before the failing step (default 10)
  --results <file>           write the results: .txt, .json, .xml (JUnit) or .md; may be repeated
  --results-template <file>  write the results with that extension as this file says, with {suite}, {passed}, {failed}, {flaky} and the like, and {flows}...{end}
  --show <a,b>               the flows the results list: failed, flaky, slow or all (default all)
  --slowest <n>              how many flows the slow list has (default 5)
  --timings                  while it runs: each step's time, each runFlow's total, the slowest steps and flows, and a note while a step hangs

Options of test and live: mocks from the real backend
  --capture <folder>         call the real backend, and write what it answers as mocks; in live, on .quit, without the calls of steps that failed
  --capture-update <folder>  capture into folder/.update, and say what changed from the mocks in folder; rayo mocks apply takes it. Given a suite instead, the folder is the flow's mock
  --check                    with --capture-update, fail if the mocks differ from the backend, and change nothing
  --capture-append           go on with the capture already in the folder, as if in one go
  --redact-value <name=value> what a private field of a body becomes, such as phone=+4915100000000 (default one of the same form: a date stays a date); again for more

Options of test, live and mocks: how a capture or an import becomes mocks
  --capture-from <url>       the backend, if calls don't begin with /host/
  --graphql <match>          tell GraphQL calls apart by operation+variables (default), by operation, or off, as any call
  --graphql-path <regex>     paths of GraphQL calls, besides those whose body has query or operationName (default .*/graphql)
  --rest <match>             match other calls by their body too (body, default), or by method and address alone (off)
  --ignore-params <a,b>      names in the query not to match, such as session or depart_at
  --ignore-body <a,b>        names, or paths such as trip.departAt, in JSON bodies and GraphQL variables, and names in forms, not to match
  --timestamps <match>       match dates and times in the query and bodies by their form (format, default), or exactly
  --capture-headers <a,b>    headers of the request to match too, such as Accept-Language
  --ignore-host              match calls whose path begins with a host, whatever the host
  --ignore-path-ids          match UUIDs and ULIDs in paths by their form, as they are new on each run
  --stateless <a,b>          paths such as api.shop.com/quotes/** whose calls only read, whatever the method: they don't change the state (* any text but /, ** any)

Options of test, live and ca: how calls reach the mock
  --network <way>            interceptor, the app sends them, with code in its debug build (default, or the flow's); proxy, the device's proxy does, no code; see rayo help connect-mocks
  --ignore-unmocked <a,b>    calls without a mock that don't fail the flow, answered 404: graphql:Operation, host/path, host or /path (* any text but /, ** any)
  --ca <folder>              with a proxy, the CA it signs with, its ca.pem and ca-key.pem (default .rayo/ca next to the suite or above it, else ~/.rayo); see rayo ca
  --hosts <a,b>              with a proxy, the hosts to open, and their subdomains (default: capturing, all but Google's, Firebase's, analytics and crash reports; else those of the mocks)

Options of live
  --app <package>            of a flow that isn't there yet
  --mock <a,b>               its mocks, relative to it
  --no-run                   don't begin by running the steps it has
  --serve                    only take commands from rayo do, until .quit

Options of mocks
  --only <a,b>               the changes whose name has one of these, such as graphql:Wallet or GET /profile (default all)
  --prune                    also take out the mocks that weren't called

Options of do
  --screen[=changes]         also what is on screen afterwards; --screen=changes, only the lines that appeared (+) or went (-) since the screen the session last gave
  --ignore-screen <regex>    with --screen, leave out the lines that match, such as a clock's; says how many
  --timeout <duration>       how long to wait for the answer, such as 30s (default as long as it takes); the session goes on
  --discard                  with .quit, end even if steps were not saved

Options of test, check, explain, devices, hierarchy, do and mocks
  --format <how>             human (default); json, for a program, see rayo schema; ndjson, the same on one line, and for test an event a line as it runs
.fi
.SH FLOW
.nf
A flow begins with a header, then ---, then a list of commands. The header:

  appId            package                    The app's
  name             text                       Shown in the output (default: the file's, or the folder's for flow.yaml)
  tags             a list                     To choose flows
  env              values                     Variables for it
  mock             a path or a list           Who answers as the backend; ${...} too, where an empty path loads nothing
  network          interceptor or proxy       How the app's calls reach the mock; ${...} too, such as ${NETWORK} from -e, where empty is the default (default: interceptor, or --network)
  record           true, false or a file      A video of the flow (default: the suite's)
  onFlowStart      commands                   Run first
  onFlowComplete   commands                   Run last, also after a failure

Commands: assertNotVisible, assertRequest, assertTrue, assertVisible, back, camera, clearState, copyTextFrom, doubleTapOn, eraseText, evalScript, extendedWaitUntil, hideKeyboard, http, inputRandomEmail, inputRandomNumber, inputRandomPersonName, inputRandomText, inputText, killApp, launchApp, longPressOn, mock, mockState, network, openLink, pasteText, pressKey, repeat, retry, runFlow, runScript, scroll, scrollUntilVisible, setAirplaneMode, setLocation, setOrientation, setPermissions, shell, startRecording, stopApp, stopRecording, swipe, takeScreenshot, tapOn, travel, type, waitForAnimationToEnd, waitForRequest
.fi
.SH SUITE
.nf
A suite, *.suite.yaml, lists flows that run together, and is where a run's settings go. Paths in it are relative to it. An option of the same name in kebab-case overrides a key for one run (failureWindow, --failure-window). A folder is the flows directly in it; a suite runs only when its file is given:

  name             text                       Shown in the results (default: the file)
  flows            a list                     Files, run in this order; or mappings with file, retries, mock, network, unmocked and capture (required)
  retries          a number from 0            How many times a flow that fails is tried again (default: 1)
  app              a mapping                  Installed before the flows
  device           a mapping                  How it is while the flows run
  env              values                     Variables for every flow, over a flow's own env; -e overrides one; they may use ${...}, such as ${rayo.file}
  timeoutScale     0.1 to 10                  Multiplies the default waits; --timeout-scale overrides it (default: 1)
  network          interceptor or proxy       How the app's calls reach the mock, as a flow's network; the flow's own and --network override it (default: each flow's, else interceptor)
  unmocked         a mapping                  Calls without a mock that don't fail the flow (default: none: each fails the flow)
  capture          a mapping                  How a capture calls the backend and becomes mocks, as the options of the same names, which win
  ca               folder                     --ca overrides it: the CA the proxy signs with, its ca.pem and ca-key.pem, relative to the suite; rayo ca new makes one (default: .rayo/ca next to the suite or above it, up to the repository's root; else ~/.rayo)
  output           a folder, or a mapping     What a run writes, and where: a folder, or folder, keep, video, artifacts and nameTemplate (default: .rayo where rayo runs)
  results          a file or a list           --results replaces them all: .txt, .json, .xml (JUnit) or .md
  detail           brief, normal, full        --detail overrides it: how much is printed (default: normal)
  failureWindow    seconds, from 1            --failure-window overrides it: a failure's log and calls begin this long before the failing step (default: 10)
  resultsTemplate  file                       --results-template overrides it: the results with its extension are written as it says
  show             a name or a list           --show overrides it: the flows the results list, of failed, flaky, slow, all (default: all)
  slowest          a number from 1            --slowest overrides it: how many flows the slow list has (default: 5)
  format           human, json or ndjson      What is printed; --format overrides it (default: human)
  flakyFailsBuild  true or false              --flaky-fails-build too: a run where every flow passed, some only on a retry, exits 4 (default: false: it exits 0)

flows, when not only a file:

  file             file                       The flow (required)
  retries          a number from 0            How many times it is tried again if it fails (default: the suite's)
  mock             a path or a list           Who answers as the backend, as a flow's mock, relative to the suite; the flow's own mock wins
  network          interceptor or proxy       How the app's calls reach the mock, as a flow's network; the flow's own and --network override it (default: the suite's)
  unmocked         a mapping                  Calls without a mock that don't fail the flow (default: the suite's; its calls are added to them)
  capture          a mapping                  How a capture calls the backend and becomes mocks, as the options of the same names, which win (default: the suite's; what it says wins over it)

unmocked:

  ignore           a list                     Calls that no mock answers but that don't fail the flow: each graphql:Operation, host/path, host or /path, as --ignore-unmocked, or a mapping with host, path and graphql (required)
  status           100 to 599                 What those calls are answered with (default: 404)
  body             text                       Of the answer (default: not mocked:  and the call)

an ignored call, when not text:

  host             host                       Of the call, or of its subdomains (default: any)
  path             a path                     Of the call, without the host; * is any text but /, ** any (default: any)
  graphql          a name or a list           GraphQL operations (default: any call)

output, when a mapping (rayo check says what a run would write):

  folder           folder                     Where everything goes; --output overrides it (default: .rayo where rayo runs)
  keep             all, failed, none          The files of every try (all), only of the tries that failed (failed), or none; --keep overrides it (default: all)
  video            true or false              A video of each flow whose header doesn't say record; --video overrides it (default: false)
  artifacts        a name or a list           The kinds of file written, of video, screenshot, logcat, screen, requests; --artifacts overrides it (default: all)
  nameTemplate     a template                 How the files are named in the folder; --name-template overrides it (default: {flow}_{attempt}_{kind}.{ext})

capture:

  hosts            a name or a list           As --hosts
  from             url                        As --capture-from
  graphql          operation+variables, operation, off As --graphql
  graphqlPath      regex                      As --graphql-path
  rest             body, off                  As --rest
  ignoreParams     a name or a list           As --ignore-params
  ignoreBody       a name or a list           As --ignore-body
  timestamps       format, exact              As --timestamps
  captureHeaders   a name or a list           As --capture-headers
  ignoreHost       true or false              As --ignore-host
  ignorePathIds    true or false              As --ignore-path-ids
  stateless        a path or a list           As --stateless
  redactValue      values                     As --redact-value: what a private field of a body becomes, such as phone: "+4915100000000"

app:

  id               package                    The app's (required)
  apk              file                       What to install, if the device has another. rayo doesn't build it (required)

device:

  size             pixels, such as 1080x2400  Of the screen
  dpi              72 to 1000                 Its density. With size, it says how many dp there are: 1080 pixels at 420 dpi are 411 dp
  fontScale        0.5 to 3                   Of the text; 1 is normal
  darkMode         true or false              The dark theme
.fi
.SH ASSERTNOTVISIBLE
.nf
assertNotVisible: The element isn't on screen, or goes away in time

selector:
  id                     text         The resource id, whole or after :id/; in Compose, a testTag with testTagsAsResourceId. A regular expression of the whole
  text                   text         The text, description or hint. A regular expression of the whole (short form)
  index                  number       The n-th match, from 0, top to bottom and left to right; negative counts from the end
  enabled                true/false   Whether it is enabled
  checked                true/false   Whether it is checked
  focused                true/false   Whether it has the focus
  selected               true/false   Whether it is selected
  below                  selector     Entirely below another
  above                  selector     Entirely above another
  leftOf                 selector     Entirely to the left of another
  rightOf                selector     Entirely to the right of another
  containsChild          selector     The direct parent of another
  childOf                selector     Anywhere inside another
  containsDescendants    selectors    Around all of these

options:
  label                  text         What to show instead of the command
  optional               true/false   A failure doesn't fail the flow
  timeout                time         How long it may take
.fi
.SH ASSERTREQUEST
